The Chrome extension also bundles third-party Linux components:
- linux-wasm runtime by Joel Severin: GPL-2.0-only (linux/vendor/LICENSE).
- Linux kernel: GPL-2.0, with the syscall note in linux/assets/KERNEL-COPYING.
- BusyBox: GPL-2.0 (linux/assets/BUSYBOX-LICENSE and GPL-2.0).
- musl: see linux/assets/MUSL-COPYRIGHT.
- Pi Tab's guest bridge (linux/bridge.c): GPL-2.0-only.

Pinned source revisions, local patches, and rebuild instructions are in linux/.
Export corresponding sources with scripts/export-linux-sources.sh and distribute
linux/sources/ alongside extension binaries. These components are not relicensed
under Apache-2.0. In the extension package, component licenses are in linux/.
